{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
  "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What if they had been included in the original legislation? If the appropriations riders had been included in the original legislation, would that make a difference?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So give me a one- or two-sentence distinguishing of that case from this one. Why is this one mandate -- mandating Tucker Act payment and that one wasn't? Because they both had the \"shall pay\" language."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Is it possible to think of those cases as -- as -- as cases we shouldn't rely on to the extent we usually do because -- because of the Judgment Fund? In other words, we live in a different world now?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: All right. Now, on that, I don't think you're saying, look through the statute books. Every time the statute says to any private citizen, if you do X, we shall"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Which are you saying?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the line that distinguishes those instances where the government says, we shall pay you, Mr. Private Citizen, if you do X. He does X, but the government does not have to pay him. What is the line?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the case that supports that line, that says, unless, government, you delegate to a private -- you delegate to an official the power to enter into a contract with the private citizen, unless you do that, even though you said \"shall pay,\" you don't have to. Okay. What is the case that says that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "does it by authorizing an agency to enter into contracts, which then forms a bilateral promise and performance --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. KNEEDLER",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is about subsidies for people participating in the market. They are not services rendered to the government. There is no promise by the government individualized --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Absent clear indication -- what clear indication would be required, short of a contract?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay, so the Secretary of the Treasury is going to be prosecuted criminally because of his interpretation of whether or not the funds were authorized?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0002-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF PAUL D. CLEMENT ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONERS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1023",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "58f6e45735cbbfe88839dcde3ca348bd683866fbbcc4cc183da20fb465cb0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-58f6e45735cb-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
